    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Everything Is Futile"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The words of the Teacher, , son of David, king in Jerusalem."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Absolute futility,” says the Teacher.",
          "“Absolute futility. Everything is futile.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What does a person gain for all his efforts",
          "that he labors at under the sun?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A generation goes and a generation comes,",
          "but the earth remains forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The sun rises and the sun sets;",
          "panting, it hurries back to the place",
          "where it rises."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Gusting to the south,",
          "turning to the north,",
          "turning, turning, goes the wind,",
          "and the wind returns in its cycles."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All the streams flow to the sea,",
          "yet the sea is never full;",
          "to the place where the streams flow,",
          "there they flow again."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "All things are wearisome,",
          "more than anyone can say.",
          "The eye is not satisfied by seeing",
          "or the ear filled with hearing."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What has been is what will be,",
          "and what has been done is what will be done;",
          "there is nothing new under the sun."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Can one say about anything,",
          "“Look, this is new”?",
          "It has already existed in the ages before us."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is no remembrance of those who came before;",
          "and of those who will come after",
          "there will also be no remembrance",
          "by those who follow them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Limitations of Wisdom"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I, the Teacher, have been king over Israel in Jerusalem."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I applied my mind to examine and explore through wisdom all that is done under heaven. God has given people this miserable task to keep them occupied."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have seen all the things that are done under the sun and have found everything to be futile, a pursuit of the wind. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "What is crooked cannot be straightened;",
          "what is lacking cannot be counted."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I said to myself, “See, I have amassed wisdom far beyond all those who were over Jerusalem before me, and my mind has thoroughly grasped wisdom and knowledge.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I applied my mind to know wisdom and knowledge, madness and folly; I learned that this too is a pursuit of the wind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For with much wisdom is much sorrow;",
          "as knowledge increases, grief increases."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
